    "title": "NBA playoffs schedule, TV channels, how to watch first-round games",
    "text": "April 14, 2026Updated April 21, 2026, 8:10 p.m. MTThe first round of the 2026 NBA playoffs is here.There are 16 teams still in the running to win the NBA championship this season after the NBA Play-In Tournament, eight in the Western Conference and eight in the Eastern Conference.The No. 1 through No. 8 seeds in each conference play in the first round of the NBA playoffs, which started on Saturday, April 18, and Sunday, April 19, with Game 1 of each series.Here's what we know about the NBA playoffs schedule for the first round right now. All times MST (add three hours for Eastern time).Each series is a best-of-seven series.NBA playoffs series schedules, TV channels: Knicks vs Hawks | Cavaliers vs Raptors | Nuggets vs Timberwolves | Lakers vs Rockets | Spurs vs Trail Blazers | Celtics vs 76ers | Pistons vs Magic | Thunder vs Suns | Daily schedule | First-round matchupsWatch NBA playoff games on FUBO (free trial)NBA playoff game schedule: Wednesday, April 22Game 2: No. 8 Orlando Magic at No. 1 Detroit Pistons, 4 p.m., ESPN (stream with FUBO)Game 2: No. 8 Phoenix Suns at No. 1 Oklahoma City Thunder, 6:30 p.m., ESPN (stream with FUBO)NBA playoffs series picks, predictions: Knicks vs Hawks | Cavaliers vs Raptors | Nuggets vs Timberwolves | Lakers vs Rockets | Spurs vs Trail Blazers | Celtics vs 76ers | Pistons vs Magic | Thunder vs Suns | The Republic's predictions | NBA playoff bracketNBA playoff game schedule: Thursday, April 23Game 3: No. 3 New York Knicks at No. 6 Atlanta Hawks, 4 p.m., Prime (stream with Prime Video)Game 3: No. 4 Cleveland Cavaliers at No. 5 Toronto Raptors, 5 p.m., Prime (stream with Prime Video)Game 3: No. 3 Denver Nuggets at No. 6 Minnesota Timberwolves, 6:30 p.m., Prime (stream with Prime Video)NBA playoffs odds: Knicks vs Hawks | Cavaliers vs Raptors | Nuggets vs Timberwolves | Lakers vs Rockets | Spurs vs Trail Blazers | Celtics vs 76ers | Pistons vs Magic | Thunder vs Suns | NBA championship odds | Game oddsNBA playoff game schedule: Friday, April 24Game 3: No. 2 Boston Celtics at No. 7 Philadelphia 76ers, 4 p.m., Prime (stream with Prime Video)Game 3: No. 4 Los Angeles Lakers at No. 5 Houston Rockets, 5 p.m., Prime (stream with Prime Video)Game 3: No. 2 San Antonio Spurs at No. 7 Portland Trail Blazers, 7:30 p.m., Prime (stream with Prime Video)NBA playoffs game predictions, picks: Knicks vs Hawks | Cavaliers vs Raptors | Nuggets vs Timberwolves | Lakers vs Rockets | Spurs vs Trail Blazers | Celtics vs 76ers | Pistons vs Magic | Thunder vs SunsWatch NBA playoff games on PeacockReach Jeremy Cluff at jeremy.cluff@arizonarepublic.com. Follow him on X, formerly Twitter @Jeremy_Cluff.Support local journalism: Subscribe to azcentral.com today. Sign up for azcentral Preps Now. And be sure to subscribe to our daily sports newsletters so you don't miss a thing.Our editors independently choose our recommendations. Some content is produced with paid support from a third party, however our editorial decisions remain independent. If you buy through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices and availability may change.",
